#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:2
msgid "CMP0220"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:6
msgid ""
"Languages enabled in subdirectories propagate to the top-level directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:8
msgid ""
"In CMake 4.4 and below, enabling a language with the :command:`project` "
"command or :command:`enable_language` command had some restrictions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:11
msgid ""
"It had to be called in file scope, not in a :command:`function` call nor "
"inside a :command:`block`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:13
msgid ""
"It had be called in the highest directory common to all targets using the "
"named language directly for compiling sources or indirectly through link "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:17
msgid ""
"While these restrictions could be met by enabling all needed languages in "
"the top-level directory of a project, this was not always easy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:20
msgid ""
"CMake 4.5 and above prefer to relax these restrictions so that languages "
"enabled by calls to the :command:`project` and :command:`enable_language` "
"commands in subdirectories are available to targets created in ancestor and "
"sibling directories created afterward.  This policy provides compatibility "
"with projects that have not been updated for the new behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:26
msgid ""
"One may think of an :command:`add_subdirectory` call as an effective call "
"site to :command:`enable_language` for languages enabled inside the "
"subdirectory's tree.  Similarly, for languages enabled in :command:"
"`function` and :command:`block` scopes, the function or :command:`endblock` "
"calls are effectively call sites to :command:`enable_language`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:32
msgid ""
"This policy is evaluated independently at each \"effective call site\", "
"proceeding up the stack of variable scopes to determine if the language "
"should be enabled at that level.  This propagation stops at the first "
"ancestor scope whose ``CMP0220`` is not ``NEW``.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:37
msgid ""
"cmake_policy(SET CMP0220 NEW)\n"
"\n"
"block()\n"
"  cmake_policy(SET CMP0220 OLD)\n"
"  block()\n"
"    cmake_policy(SET CMP0220 NEW)\n"
"    block()\n"
"      cmake_policy(SET CMP0220 OLD)\n"
"      enable_language(CXX)\n"
"      # CXX is enabled in this scope\n"
"    endblock()\n"
"    # CXX is enabled in this scope\n"
"  endblock()\n"
"  # CXX is not enabled in this scope\n"
"endblock()\n"
"# CXX is not enabled in this scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/STANDARD_ADVICE.rst:1
msgid ""
"This policy was introduced in CMake version |INTRODUCED_IN_CMAKE_VERSION|. "
"It may be set by :command:`cmake_policy` or :command:"
"`cmake_minimum_required`. If it is not set, CMake |WARNS_OR_DOES_NOT_WARN|, "
"and uses ``OLD`` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0220.rst:60
msgid ""
"See documentation of the :variable:`CMAKE_POLICY_WARNING_CMP0220 "
"<CMAKE_POLICY_WARNING_CMP<NNNN>>` variable to control the warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/DEPRECATED.rst:2
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior of a policy is :ref:`deprecated by definition <cmake-"
"policies-intro>` and may be removed in a future version of CMake."
msgstr ""
